From 3988022e1dc459b50eecc29a856bc495b22121e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 22:32:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/41] webserver: raise the URI handler limit so the live
 spectrum socket registers

GET + POST /api/relay brought webserver.c to 50 handlers; with 5 in
filebrowser.c and /ws in webserver_ws.c that is 56 against a limit of 55.
/ws registers last, so it was refused (ESP_ERR_HTTPD_HANDLERS_FULL) and the
web page's live spectrum never connected. Limit raised to 64, with the
three-file count recorded next to it.

Tested: /ws registers, one live session, spectrum drawn from the NAS stream.
PDF updated (fix, test, and the touch-after-flash note).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W7MAsxunucnfwkhxdqp61S
